 * @brief Create a new buffer initialized with a null-terminated string.
 *
 * Allocates a new buffer and copies the contents of the given null-terminated
 * string into it. The resulting buffer contains the string data but does not
 * include the terminating null byte.
 *
 * @param str Null-terminated string to copy into the buffer. Must not be NULL.
 *
 * @return Pointer to the newly allocated buffer on success, or NULL if memory
 *         allocation fails.
 *
 * @note Caller is responsible for freeing the returned buffer.
 * @see buffer_new_with_string_length
 */
